# Tetris Autoplayer

An AI “brain” for an existing Tetris game. The AI autonomously selects optimal moves using weighted heuristic functions and a hill-climbing algorithm to maximize gameplay performance. Only the `player.py` file (AI logic) was developed by Daniel Wheeler; the Tetris engine was provided separately.

## Features
- Developed the `player.py` AI that selects moves based on heuristics (holes, bumpiness, lines cleared)
- Implemented a hill-climbing algorithm to optimize heuristic weightings
- Integrated `player.py` with the provided Tetris engine for autonomous gameplay
- Iteratively tested and refined AI performance

## How It Works
The AI evaluates all possible moves and scores them using heuristic functions. A hill-climbing algorithm adjusts the weightings to select moves that maximize score while minimizing holes and unevenness on the board.
